You won't want to miss the Hancock County Chamber of Commerce Spring Market this Saturday, April 27th! There will be painting and mini golf activities for the whole family, and inflatables for the children. There will also be the great opportunity to support 24 local vendors, from 10 a.m. to 2 p.m. in downtown Lewisport. Paint ‘n Take The Hancock County Public Library and St. Vincent DePaul Thrift Store are sponsoring a FREE Paint ‘n Take opportunity, from 10 a.m. until 1 p.m. This fun, creative activity will be for children and adults, and involves painting on a canvas with Q-tips. Anyone at any skill level is invited to paint and can take their creation home with them! The Paint-And-Take station will be set-up near the pavilion. Classes at 10 a.m., 11 a.m. & noon. Holes-to-Go Mini Golf Financial Advisor Katie Kolonich with Edward Jones, as well as Outlaw Metalworks are sponsoring a Holes-to-Go Miniature Golf activity. The company Holes-to-Go is located in Owensboro and will be bringing their traveling, multi-hole miniature golf course for people to enjoy. This will be set-up in the grass area to the right of the Hancock County Farm Museum. Inflatables There will be 2 inflatables for the children to enjoy! One will be designated for special abilities children only. Food The list of vendors includes local food trucks with their delicious offerings. Hello Pop (Chelsea Boling) will have shake ups & pops, and EMazing Cupcakes & Treats (Emma Wilson) will offer a variety of cake cups, cookies & cake pops to choose from. Kluckies Chicken Food Truck (Ashley Laslie) will offer fried chicken, waffle fries, fried pickles & cheese cubes. Beverages Sammy J Studio will have a Competitive Dance Team Lemonade Boba Stand set-up, and Kona Ice will be vending as well. Spring Market Vendors There will be local vendors offering their various wares such as many hand-crafted items, including: For Gigi's Sake (Marie Bennett) -homemade tees & earrings;
Morris Custom Creations (Liz Morris) -tumblers, keychains, earrings, etc.;
Golden Treasures (Gail Golden) -handmade wreaths & table décor and antique tabletop glassware;
Made With Love (Kelli Shively) -cups & more;
Sealed with Love (Courtney West) -keychains, decorative pens & bracelets;
Liv's Creations (Pam Miller) -all different types of breads;
With A Little Help From My Friends (Kara Eckles)-vintage thrift shop;
Felts Farm (Jennifer Felts) -crochet toys, sourdough breads, yeast breads & cakes;
Two Twisted Sisters, LLC (Rachel Johnson) -sister crafted, handmade jewelry & crochet;
Drools And Jewels (Ashley Bradshaw) -permanent jewelry and Plunder Jewelry;
Two Crafty Gals (Carlotta Luna) -crochet items, sewn items, handmade candies, wooden shelf items, plant hangers & macramé;
NeNe Hamilton's Creations (Beth Hamilton) -Baby taggies, fabric topped hanging towels, plastic canvas items & possibly kid-created crafts;
Pinky's Prints (Tammy Pinkston) -3D Prints;
The Little Healer, LLC (Michelle Hoover) -calendula salve, magnesium spray, comfrey salve, Ease Away herbal pain reliever, bamboo products, homemade laundry detergent, wool laundry balls, lip balms & handmade perfumes;
Seven Sisters (Ethel Wheatley) -t-shirts, framed prints, quilts & home décor;
Hope's Bling Boutique (Hope Collier) -$5 jewelry;
Peace, Love and Bell Bottoms (Lisa McDaniel) -beaded & wire jewelry including bracelets & necklaces;
Midnight Oil Custom Laser Engraving (Kaylie Fullenwider) -laser engraving of wood, acrylic & metal items & taking orders for custom items. Information Booths at Spring Market
Melissa Miles Walker with OASIS Shelter, non-profit domestic violence shelter/agency, will have an information booth regarding their services, as well as a fun game for children to play and win a sweet prize. Hancock County Program Manager Robin Gaynor with CASA of Ohio Valley will have an information booth set-up as well. Court Appointed Special Advocates (CASA) is currently seeking individuals to volunteer as advocates for children in the HC Court system. By Jennifer Wimmer
